# gate/generated.manifest — files that are PROJECTIONS, and who projects them.
#
# A generated file edited by hand is the most durable kind of wrong answer in
# this repository: the edit works, the tests pass, and the next generator run
# silently deletes it. Worse, the hand edit becomes the de facto authority
# while the generator -- the actual source of truth -- keeps saying something
# else.
#
# THE RULE, enforced by gate/layering.sh:
#   (1) A generated file must still carry its do-not-edit marker. Deleting the
#       marker is the first move of anyone about to author inside one.
#   (2) A diff that touches a generated file must touch its generator in the
#       same diff. If the generator did not change, the projection had no
#       reason to.
#
# FORMAT:  <generated-path>\t<generator-path>\t<marker-substring>

src/lexer_tokenize.c	lib/compiler/lexer.id	do not edit
src/keyword_classify.c	src/token_classify_gen.zig	do not edit by hand
lib/token/classify.id	src/token_classify_gen.zig	do not edit by hand
src/grammar_role_table.zig	lib/compiler/token.id	do not edit by hand
lib/token/grammarrole.id	lib/compiler/token.id	do not edit by hand
lib/wasm/opcode_lookup.id	src/wasm_semantic_gen.zig	do not edit by hand
lib/wasm/ward_mvp_opcodes.id	src/wasm_semantic_gen.zig	do not edit by hand
ext/tree-sitter-idol/grammar.js	scripts/treesitter_emit.id	GENERATED
tools/wasm/src/duo_keyword_classify.c	src/token_classify_gen.zig	do not edit by hand
tools/lsp/src/duo_keyword_classify.c	src/token_classify_gen.zig	do not edit by hand
